{
  "info": {
    "name": "NY WhatsApp Regular Ride Flow (Bangalore, Auto Rickshaw)",
    "description": "End-to-end Regular (one-way) ride booked entirely through the WhatsApp bot's real webhook, driver side unchanged from EasyBookingRideFlow:\n  Driver onboard -> WA: ride_type:regular -> WA: pickup pin -> WA: pickup_confirm -> WA: drop pin -> WA: regular_book (fires select2 in the background) -> driver accepts -> driver starts -> end ride -> verify completed.\n\nScope: ride mechanics only. This does NOT assert WhatsApp message content/buttons, and does NOT exercise the background tracker's assigned/arrived/started/ended pushes (Tracker.hs) - those all require a Meta Graph API mock, which is out of scope here. Outbound sends will still fire for real against https://graph.facebook.com using whatever's in meta_config and will most likely fail (no valid access token) - that's expected and non-fatal (WhatsappBot.Adapter.Sender.sendSafe swallows the error).\n\nEach WA step POSTs a simulated Meta webhook envelope to {{webhook_base_url}}/webhook/whatsapp, signed with X-Hub-Signature-256 computed in the prerequest script using {{whatsapp_app_secret}} - this MUST match the plaintext meta_config.app_secret for {{whatsapp_phone_number_id}} in the local DB (see config-sync/assets/patches.json's meta_config override; run config_transfer.py import before this collection or the signature check will reject every WA step with a non-2xx).\n\nEnvelope shapes copied verbatim from lib/whatsapp-bot/test/resources/golden/regular-happy-path.json (the real recorded fixture for this exact scenario). Driver-side steps copied from EasyBookingRideFlow/01-EasyBookingRideFlow.json.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "exec": [
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('_test_driver_number')) {",
          "    var dNum = '9' + Math.floor(100000000 + Math.random() * 899999999);",
          "    var rNum = '8' + Math.floor(100000000 + Math.random() * 899999999);",
          "    var regNo = 'KA' + String(Math.floor(10 + Math.random() * 89)) + String.fromCharCode(65 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 26)) + String.fromCharCode(65 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 26)) + String(Math.floor(1000 + Math.random() * 8999));",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('_test_driver_number', dNum);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('_test_rider_number', rNum);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('_test_reg_no', regNo);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('_wa_msg_seq', '0');",
          "    console.log('Test driver:', dNum, 'rider:', rNum, 'reg:', regNo);",
          "}"
        ],
        "type": "text/javascript"
      }
    }
  ],
